  "subsections": [
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "summary": "What this topic covers.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "topic-map",
          "html": "<p>A password is still the front door to almost every account you have. Most break-ins don't come from someone guessing a clever password &mdash; they come from <b>reused</b> passwords leaked in one breach and tried everywhere else. The fix is simple: a different, long, random password for every account, kept in a password manager, with two-factor authentication on the accounts that matter most.</p>"
        }
      ]
